<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  {#- Same title on every version: Chrome copies it into the PDF's properties,
      and an employer should never see "Federal" or "Tailored" there. #}
  <title>{{ site.name }}: Resume</title>
  <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
  {#- Self-contained on purpose: the CSS is inline and every link is a full
      address, so scripts/resume-pdf.js can print the page straight from disk
      without a local path ending up in the PDF. The font is Arial (Patrick's
      choice); Arimo, loaded below, has Arial's exact measurements, so a computer
      without Arial (like GitHub's Linux runners) lays the PDF out the same. #}
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Arimo:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&display=block">
  <style>
{% include "css/resume-print.css" %}
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="sheet">
{{ content | safe }}
</main>
</body>
</html>
